# @Callable permits calling with multiple arguments (B-673 regression guard).
# f@Callable annotates a parameter as "some function" (variadic=true, zero fixed params).
# The function should be callable with any number of arguments without a spurious arity
# mismatch type error. Verifies constrain_fn allows Callable to accept any concrete fn signature.

[
  apply: [fn [let f@Callable a b] [f a b]]
  result: [apply [fn [let x y] [+ x y]] 1 2]
]
=== out
Dict({"apply": Function(f, a, b), "result": Int(3)})
